Z||000006||Uaana||07-29-2001||05:38 PM||||Well like Songman said alot of what he said it true. You have to find what you like to really make a decision. <BR>Myself I like a nice light Shiraz with steaks. Reislings I would only serve with fruit theyre just a little too sweet for my taste. <BR>If you want to take a safe bet that will somewhat satisfy most people. <BR>Try a decent Merlot for Italian (Robert Mondavi reserve, maybe something from the coastal line)<BR>For seafood try a neutral Pinot Greigo like Cavit.<P>And If I have gotten any of these spellings incorrect sorry. Just know where they are in the store I work at.. Thank god for wine tasting on Fri's now I have at least a general idea of what the heck I'm talking about.||||reg||1
