Z||000014||LarryB||07-30-2001||01:58 PM||||Unfortunately, no. The lawyers would have a field day if for example I served alcohol to someone under 21 who then went out and wrapped his/her car around a telephone pole.  <BR>When I turned legal age it was still 18 down here.  I don't know if they've accomplished very much by raising it back to 21, other than it giving the politicians something to crow about because they "did something about the problem". <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Thats why Canada is so much better. 19 sounds fine to me. But we have a law that underage people can drink in your home if you are there supervising.. You guys don't have that?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||JohnnyK||07-30-2001||02:06 PM||||Well yeah, you'd still get in trouble if someoen wrapped their car around a pole, but say a young kid was staying there, you are allowed to serve him alcohol (say for dinner or something right?).||||reg||1
Z||000016||Steve Normington||07-30-2001||03:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LarryB:<BR><B>When I turned legal age it was still 18 down here.  I don't know if they've accomplished very much by raising it back to 21, other than it giving the politicians something to crow about because they "did something about the problem". </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually they did. It used to be that each state would set the legal drinking age. So college aged kids in a high age state would drive to the state border of a lower age state, get hammered and then drive back. Now that the age is the same, they get one older kid to buy for everyone and get hammered at home.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Voytek||07-30-2001||04:05 PM||||i.e. means 'that is'.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||MrPBody||07-30-2001||10:23 PM||||Try a lot of wines; try to remember what you like.  As a practicing cheapskate, I shy away from $$well-known$$ California and French brands.  I find it hard to appreciate a wine that costs more than about $10 in a liquor store, or $25-$30 in a restaurant.  I like some Northwest wines such as Hogue, Columbia Crest, Chateau St. Michelle, and Duck Pond.  Australia also produces some nice inexpensive wines: Jacobs Creek and Lindemans, for instance.  And some Chilean reds are quite good and dirt cheap.  Believe it or not, there are even some good Georgia wines.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||artherd||07-31-2001||01:23 AM||||Gosh, where to start!?  I could probally fill an entire Pennock's page with just one post here, but I will spare you :)<P>I love Sonoma/Napa county (California) wines, indeed I've probally worked for more than half of them :P<P>My advice is simply; go to resturants, try *everything* get different wines with different foods, ALWAYS make them tell you the wine, get them to bring the bottle out so you can look at it.    The good ones will stick in your head, so seek them out for your home collection!!<P>Best place to keep wine is a constant-temprature cool and dry <BR>area. Temprature STABILITY is most important, though it should never get over 85-90degreesF.  If you at all can, I suggest investing in a refirgerator regulated speficically for wines, they will last.<P> Keep the corks lubricated <BR>(ie, store on their sides, NEVER upright!!)<BR>Reds age forever, whites are gone in 10-15 years, so enjoy it while it lasts!<P><BR>Above ALL, do what you like with wine!  If you want a Cabernet with Fillet of Sole, do it!!  If you want a Zinfindel while working out and eating Prime Rib, do it!! ;)<P>Wine is great fun, the next step for me is going to be planting some vines very soon, wish me luck guys!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
